text: ['({T}: Add {B}.)', '({T}: Add {G}.)', '({T}: Add {R}.)', '({T}: Add {U}.)', '({T}: Add {W}.)', 'All creatures able to block Prized Unicorn do so.', "As Pithing Needle enters the battlefield, choose a card name.\\nActivated abilities of sources with the chosen name can't be activated unless they're mana abilities.", "At the beginning of each player's draw step, if Howling Mine is untapped, that player draws an additional card.", "At the beginning of your upkeep, choose target nonland permanent you control and up to two target nonland permanents you don't control. Destroy one of them at random.", 'At the beginning of your upkeep, create a 2/2 green Wolf creature token.\\n{T}: Tap all untapped Wolf creatures you control. Each Wolf tapped this way deals damage equal to its power to target creature. That creature deals damage equal to its power divided as its controller chooses among any number of those Wolves.', 'Attacking creatures get +2/+0 until end of turn.', 'Berserkers of Blood Ridge attacks each combat if able.', 'Copy target instant or sorcery spell. You may choose new targets for the copy.', 'Counter target creature spell.', 'Counter target noncreature spell.', 'Counter target red or green spell.', 'Counter target spell.', 'Create a 2/2 green Wolf creature token for each Forest you control.', 'Creatures you control gain haste until end of turn. (They can attack and {T} even if they just came under your control.)', 'Creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Creatures you control get +3/+3 and gain trample until end of turn.', 'Creatures you control have flying.', 'Deathtouch (Any amount of damage this deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)\\nWhen Acidic Slime enters the battlefield, destroy target artifact, enchantment, or land.', "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\n{B}: Regenerate Wall of Bone. (The next time this creature would be destroyed this turn, it isn't. Instead tap it, remove all damage from it, and remove it from combat.)", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\n{R}: Wall of Fire gets +1/+0 until end of turn.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\n{W}: Wall of Faith gets +0/+1 until end of turn.", "Defender\\nWhenever Wall of Frost blocks a creature, that creature doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", 'Destroy all enchantments.', 'Destroy all nonland permanents.', 'Destroy target artifact or enchantment.', 'Destroy target artifact or enchantment. You gain 4 life.', 'Destroy target artifact.', 'Destroy target attacking or blocking creature.', "Destroy target creature. It can't be regenerated. Its controller reveals cards from the top of their library until they reveal a creature card. The player puts that card onto the battlefield, then shuffles all other cards revealed this way into their library.", 'Destroy target green or white creature.', 'Destroy target nonblack creature.', 'Destroy target tapped creature.', 'Dragonskull Summit enters the battlefield tapped unless you control a Swamp or a Mountain.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {R}.', 'Draw X cards.', 'Draw two cards.', "Dread Warlock can't be blocked except by black creatures.", 'Drowned Catacomb enters the battlefield tapped unless you control an Island or a Swamp.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {B}.', 'Each creature gets +1/+1 for each other creature on the battlefield that shares at least one creature type with it. (For example, if two Goblin Warriors and a Goblin Shaman are on the battlefield, each gets +2/+2.)', 'Each opponent sacrifices a land.', 'Each player draws three cards, then discards three cards at random.', "Each player shuffles all permanents they own into their library, then reveals that many cards from the top of their library. Each player puts all artifact, creature, and land cards revealed this way onto the battlefield, then does the same for enchantment cards, then puts all cards revealed this way that weren't put onto the battlefield on the bottom of their library.", 'Earthquake deals X damage to each creature without flying and each player.', "Enchant creature\\nAt the beginning of the upkeep of enchanted creature's controller, that player loses 1 life.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't attack or block, and its activated abilities can't be activated.\\nWhen enchanted creature becomes the target of a spell or ability, destroy Ice Cage.", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't attack or block.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+1 for each Plains you control and has flying.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+2.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+1.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +3/+3.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets -2/-1.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has lifelink. (Damage dealt by the creature also causes its controller to gain that much life.)', 'Enchant creature\\nYou control enchanted creature.', 'Enchant creature\\n{R}: Enchanted creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Enchant land\\nAs Convincing Mirage enters the battlefield, choose a basic land type.\\nEnchanted land is the chosen type.', 'Enchant permanent\\nEnchanted permanent has indestructible. (Effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy that permanent. A creature with indestructible can\'t be destroyed by damage.)', "Enchant tapped creature\\nEnchanted creature doesn't untap during its controller's untap step.", "Equipped creature can't be blocked and has shroud. (It can't be the target of spells or abilities.)\\nEquip {2}", 'Equipped creature gets +1/+1 and has deathtouch. (Any amount of damage it deals to a creature is enough to destroy that creature.)\\nEquip {2} ({2}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', 'Equipped creature gets +2/+4 and loses flying.\\nPrevent all noncombat damage that would be dealt to equipped creature.\\nEquip {2} ({2}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', "Exile all cards from target player's graveyard other than basic land cards. For each card exiled this way, search that player's library for all cards with the same name as that card and exile them. Then that player shuffles.", 'Exile target black or red permanent.', 'First strike (This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)', 'First strike (This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)\\nOther Soldier creatures you control have first strike.', "First strike (This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)\\nProtection from black (This creature can't be blocked, targeted, dealt damage, or enchanted by anything black.)", "First strike (This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)\\nProtection from white (This creature can't be blocked, targeted, dealt damage, or enchanted by anything white.)", 'First strike (This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)\\nWhenever Lightwielder Paladin deals combat damage to a player, you may exile target black or red permanent that player controls.', 'Flash\\nFlying\\nWhen Bogardan Hellkite enters the battlefield, it deals 5 damage divided as you choose among any number of targets.', 'Flying', "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nFirst strike (This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nNightmare's power and toughness are each equal to the number of Swamps you control.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\n{R}: Shivan Dragon gets +1/+0 until end of turn.", 'Flying, first strike, lifelink, protection from Demons and from Dragons', "Flying, trample\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice a creature other than Xathrid Demon, then each opponent loses life equal to the sacrificed creature's power. If you can't sacrifice a creature, tap Xathrid Demon and you lose 7 life.", 'Flying, vigilance', "Flying\\nDjinn of Wishes enters the battlefield with three wish counters on it.\\n{2}{U}{U}, Remove a wish counter from Djinn of Wishes: Reveal the top card of your library. You may play that card without paying its mana cost. If you don't, exile it.", 'Flying\\nIf a source an opponent controls would deal damage to you, prevent 1 of that damage.', "Flying\\nVigilance (Attacking doesn't cause this creature to tap.)", 'Flying\\nWhen Howling Banshee enters the battlefield, each player loses 3 life.', 'Flying\\nWhen Illusionary Servant becomes the target of a spell or ability, sacrifice it.', 'Flying\\nWhen Magma Phoenix dies, it deals 3 damage to each creature and each player.\\n{3}{R}{R}: Return Magma Phoenix from your graveyard to your hand.', 'Flying\\nWhen Sage Owl enters the battlefield, look at the top four cards of your library, then put them back in any order.', 'Flying\\nWhenever Hypnotic Specter deals damage to an opponent, that player discards a card at random.', "Flying\\nWhenever Sphinx Ambassador deals combat damage to a player, search that player's library for a card, then that player chooses a card name. If you searched for a creature card that doesn't have that name, you may put it onto the battlefield under your control. Then that player shuffles.", "Flying\\nYou can't lose the game and your opponents can't win the game.", 'Flying\\n{R}: Dragon Whelp gets +1/+0 until end of turn. If this ability has been activated four or more times this turn, sacrifice Dragon Whelp at the beginning of the next end step.', 'Flying\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color.', "Forestwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Forest.)", 'Gain control of target creature until end of turn. Untap that creature. It gains haste until end of turn. (It can attack and {T} this turn.)', 'Glacial Fortress enters the battlefield tapped unless you control a Plains or an Island.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {U}.', 'Haste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)', 'Haste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)\\nOther Goblin creatures you control get +1/+1 and have haste.', 'Ignite Disorder deals 3 damage divided as you choose among one, two, or three target white and/or blue creatures.', "Jackal Familiar can't attack or block alone.", 'Lava Axe deals 5 damage to target player or planeswalker.', 'Lifelink', 'Lightning Bolt deals 3 damage to any target.', 'Look at the top three cards of your library, then put them back in any order. You may shuffle.\\nDraw a card.', 'Other Elf creatures you control get +1/+1.\\n{T}: Add {G} for each Elf you control.', "Other Merfolk creatures you control get +1/+1.\\n{T}: Target Merfolk creature can't be blocked this turn.", 'Other Soldier creatures you control get +0/+1.', 'Other Soldier creatures you control get +1/+0.', 'Other Zombie creatures you control get +1/+1.\\n{2}{B}, {T}: Exile target creature card from a graveyard. Create a 2/2 black Zombie creature token.', 'Palace Guard can block any number of creatures.', "Phantom Warrior can't be blocked.", 'Play with the top card of your library revealed.\\nAs long as the top card of your library is black, Vampire Nocturnus and other Vampire creatures you control get +2/+1 and have flying.', 'Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn.', 'Prevent all damage that would be dealt to you and creatures you control this turn.', 'Protean Hydra enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it.\\nIf damage would be dealt to Protean Hydra, prevent that damage and remove that many +1/+1 counters from it.\\nWhenever a +1/+1 counter is removed from Protean Hydra, put two +1/+1 counters on it at the beginning of the next end step.', 'Put target creature card from a graveyard onto the battlefield under your control. That creature is a black Zombie in addition to its other colors and types.', "Put target creature on top of its owner's library.", 'Pyroclasm deals 2 damage to each creature.', 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)', 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)\\nDeathtouch (Any amount of damage this deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)', "Regenerate target creature. (The next time that creature would be destroyed this turn, it isn't. Instead tap it, remove all damage from it, and remove it from combat.)", 'Relentless Rats gets +1/+1 for each other creature on the battlefield named Relentless Rats.\\nA deck can have any number of cards named Relentless Rats.', "Return all artifact and enchantment cards from all graveyards to the battlefield under their owners' control. (Auras with nothing to enchant remain in graveyards.)", 'Return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', "Return target creature to its owner's hand.", 'Return target permanent card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'Rootbound Crag enters the battlefield tapped unless you control a Mountain or a Forest.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {G}.', 'Sacrifice a creature: Vampire Aristocrat gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for a card, put that card into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for an artifact card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Seismic Strike deals damage to target creature equal to the number of Mountains you control.', "Serpent of the Endless Sea's power and toughness are each equal to the number of Islands you control.\\nSerpent of the Endless Sea can't attack unless defending player controls an Island.", "Shroud (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", 'Spend only black mana on X.\\nConsume Spirit deals X damage to any target and you gain X life.', 'Sunpetal Grove enters the battlefield tapped unless you control a Forest or a Plains.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {W}.', "Swampwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Swamp.)", "Tap all creatures target player controls. Those creatures don't untap during that player's next untap step.", 'Target blocking creature gets +7/+7 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gains flying until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +1/+0 and gains first strike until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +3/+3 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +7/+7 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets -7/-0 until end of turn.', 'Target opponent reveals their hand. You choose a noncreature, nonland card from it. That player discards that card.', 'Target player discards X cards at random.', 'Target player discards two cards.', 'Target player draws two cards and loses 2 life.', 'Target player mills five cards.', 'Target player mills half their library, rounded down.', 'Target player takes an extra turn after this one.', 'Tendrils of Corruption deals X damage to target creature and you gain X life, where X is the number of Swamps you control.', 'The next 2 damage that a source of your choice would deal to you and/or permanents you control this turn is dealt to any target instead.', "This spell can't be countered.\\nProtection from blue and from black (This creature can't be blocked, targeted, dealt damage, or enchanted by anything blue or black.)", 'This spell costs {1} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nFireball deals X damage divided evenly, rounded down, among any number of targets.', "Trample (This creature can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)", "Trample (This creature can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)\\nHaste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)\\nAt the beginning of the end step, sacrifice Ball Lightning.", "Trample, indestructible\\nIf Darksteel Colossus would be put into a graveyard from anywhere, reveal Darksteel Colossus and shuffle it into its owner's library instead.", "Up to three target creatures can't block this turn.", "Vigilance (Attacking doesn't cause this creature to tap.)\\nOther Soldier creatures you control get +1/+1 and have vigilance.\\nWhen Captain of the Watch enters the battlefield, create three 1/1 white Soldier creature tokens.", "When Awakener Druid enters the battlefield, target Forest becomes a 4/5 green Treefolk creature for as long as Awakener Druid remains on the battlefield. It's still a land.", 'When Borderland Ranger enters the battlefield, you may search your library for a basic land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'When Elvish Visionary enters the battlefield, draw a card.', 'When Gravedigger enters the battlefield, you may return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Siege-Gang Commander enters the battlefield, create three 1/1 red Goblin creature tokens.\\n{1}{R}, Sacrifice a Goblin: Siege-Gang Commander deals 2 damage to any target.', 'When Sparkmage Apprentice enters the battlefield, it deals 1 damage to any target.', 'Whenever Bramble Creeper attacks, it gets +5/+0 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Inferno Elemental blocks or becomes blocked by a creature, Inferno Elemental deals 3 damage to that creature.', 'Whenever a player casts a black spell, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts a blue spell, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts a green spell, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts a red spell, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts a white spell, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts an instant or sorcery spell, each other player copies that spell. Each of those players may choose new targets for their copy.', 'Whenever a player taps a land for mana, Manabarbs deals 1 damage to that player.', 'Whenever an opponent casts a blue or black spell, you may put a +1/+1 counter on Mold Adder.', "Whenever an opponent casts a spell, reveal the top card of your library. If it's a creature card, put it onto the battlefield. Otherwise, you may put that card on the bottom of your library.", 'Whenever an opponent discards a card, Megrim deals 2 damage to that player.', 'Whenever an opponent draws a card, Underworld Dreams deals 1 damage to that player.', 'Whenever another creature enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.', 'Whenever you cast an enchantment spell, you may draw a card.', 'Whenever you gain life, target opponent loses that much life.', 'White creatures you control get +1/+1.', 'Windstorm deals X damage to each creature with flying.', 'You gain 1 life for each land you control.', 'You gain 7 life.', 'You have no maximum hand size.', 'You may have Clone enter the battlefield as a copy of any creature on the battlefield.', "Your opponents can't cast spells this turn.", 'Your opponents play with their hands revealed.', "[+1]: Chandra Nalaar deals 1 damage to target player or planeswalker.\\n[−X]: Chandra Nalaar deals X damage to target creature.\\n[−8]: Chandra Nalaar deals 10 damage to target player or planeswalker and each creature that player or that planeswalker's controller controls.", '[+1]: Target player discards a card.\\n[−2]: Search your library for a card, then shuffle and put that card on top.\\n[−8]: Put all creature cards from all graveyards onto the battlefield under your control.', '[+1]: Untap two target lands.\\n[−1]: Create a 3/3 green Beast creature token.\\n[−4]: Creatures you control get +3/+3 and gain trample until end of turn.', '[+1]: You gain 2 life.\\n[−1]: Put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control. Those creatures gain vigilance until end of turn.\\n[−6]: Create a white Avatar creature token. It has "This creature\'s power and toughness are each equal to your life total."', '[+2]: Each player draws a card.\\n[−1]: Target player draws a card.\\n[−10]: Target player mills twenty cards.', '{1}{B}, {T}: Target player loses 1 life.', '{1}{G}: Create a 1/1 green Insect creature token.', '{3}, {T}: Rod of Ruin deals 1 damage to any target.', '{B}: Looming Shade gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', "{B}: Regenerate Drudge Skeletons. (The next time this creature would be destroyed this turn, it isn't. Instead tap it, remove all damage from it, and remove it from combat.)", '{G}, {T}: You may put a creature card from your hand onto the battlefield.', "{G}: Regenerate Cudgel Troll. (The next time this creature would be destroyed this turn, it isn't. Instead tap it, remove all damage from it, and remove it from combat.)", '{R}: Fiery Hellhound gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', '{T}, Sacrifice Mirror of Fate: Choose up to seven face-up exiled cards you own. Exile all the cards from your library, then put the chosen cards on top of your library.', '{T}, Sacrifice Terramorphic Expanse: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{5}, {T}, Sacrifice Gargoyle Castle: Create a 3/4 colorless Gargoyle artifact creature token with flying.', '{T}: Add {G}.', '{T}: Destroy target tapped creature.', '{T}: Draw a card, then discard a card.', '{T}: Goblin Artillery deals 2 damage to any target and 3 damage to you.', '{T}: Prodigal Pyromancer deals 1 damage to any target.', '{T}: Target creature an opponent controls attacks you this turn if able.', "{T}: Target creature you control with toughness less than Stone Giant's power gains flying until end of turn. Destroy that creature at the beginning of the next end step.", '{W}, {T}: Exile target Skeleton, Vampire, or Zombie.', '{W}, {T}: Tap target creature.']
flavor: ['"A flash of the lightning, a break of the wave,\\nHe passes from life to his rest in the grave."\\n—William Knox, "Mortality"', '"A relic donation is suggested."\\n"The suggestion is mandatory."\\n—Temple signs', '"All consciousness is one, separated only by a thin veil of the physical."\\n—Jace Beleren', '"All the wizardry in the world has to pass through one small and easily sealed door."\\n—Ajani Goldmane', '"At summer\'s end, the pegasus herd stampedes across the sky. Their silent footfalls taunt the clouds and bid the rains to come."\\n—Stormfront fable', '"Blood is constant. Every drop I drink, someone must bleed."\\n—Vradeen, vampire nocturnus', '"Born under the moon, the second child will stumble on temptation and seek power in the dark places of the heart."\\n—Codex of the Constellari', '"Born under the sun, the first child will seek the foundation of honor and be fortified by its righteousness."\\n—Codex of the Constellari', '"Catch!"', '"Courage is a proud and gleaming shield. It does not bend or hide from sight. To fight with courage, we must forge in steel."', '"Death is no excuse for disobedience."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"Defending the citadel is easy. I just take these big fellows outside the main gate and let the enemy take a good long look."\\n—Mastodon keeper', '"Do not fire upon it—it is bad luck. And a waste of arrows."\\n—Alera Benath, Kalonian ranger', '"Don\'t worry. I\'m not going to deprive you of all your secrets. Just your most precious one."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"Everything the wise woman learned she wrote in a book, and when the pages were black with ink, she took white ink and began again."\\n—Karn, silver golem', '"For strength to have any meaning, there must also be . . . you."', '"Humanity has always envied the power of flight. So we took it."\\n—Scytha, aeromage', '"I admit, I am a creature of the city. The sights, the nightly excitement, the abundance of fine drink . . ."', '"I can\'t claim to hunt all creatures. There are some things in the jungle that simply can\'t be hunted."\\n—Garruk Wildspeaker', '"I carry the light of truth. Do not pity those it blinds, for they never had eyes to see."', '"I don\'t know who to pity more: those who flee from my presence or the damned who can withstand it."', '"I don\'t know why people say a double-edged sword is bad. It\'s a sword. With two edges."\\n—Kamahl, pit fighter', '"I fear no army or beast, but only the morning fog. Our assault can survive everything else."\\n—Lord Hilneth', '"I give them dreams so wondrous that they hesitate to return to the world of the conscious."\\n—Garild, merfolk mage', '"I welcome it. The pasture is cleared of weeds and the wolves are frozen solid."\\n—Lumi, goatherd', '"I\'m not nearly as bothered by being outnumbered as I am by their foul stench."', '"I\'m one masterpiece away from ruling this pathetic world."\\n—Saldrath, master artificer', '"I\'ve never understood why so many beings lumber around on the ground. There are three dimensions, yet they use only two."', '"I\'ve seen the fully grown ones tear a baloth to gory ribbons in seconds."\\n—Kivi, thornberry harvester', '"If it has a brain, even a primitive one, we can most surely scramble it."\\n—Garild, merfolk mage', '"Illusion is a handy but fragile medium. Use it only in a pinch, or against the dim-witted."\\n—Jace Beleren', '"In the drowsy dark cave of the mind, dreams build their nest with fragments dropped from day\'s caravan."\\n—Rabindranath Tagore', '"It\'s a vicious circle. Stress breeds pain. Pain breeds stress. It\'s simply beautiful, wouldn\'t you agree?"\\n—Vradeen, vampire nocturnus', '"Kill the queen first, or we\'ll be fighting her drones forever. It is not in a queen\'s nature to have enough servants."\\n—Borzard, exterminator captain', '"Let everything return to its true nature, so that destiny may take its course."', '"Let the gray-hairs keep their ravens and drakes. My familiar will be a reflection of me: bloodthirsty, with a predator\'s instinct."\\n—Taivang, barbarian warlord', '"Life up here is simple. Adapt to the ways of the mountains and they will reward you. Fight them and they will end you."\\n—Kezim, prodigal pyromancer', '"My masterpiece is complete—and so shall be my triumph."\\n—Saldrath, master artificer', '"My motive is not vengeance but mercy. I deliver the soulless back to their severed souls."', '"One does not question the size or shape of the grains of sand in an hourglass. Nor do I question the temperament of the souls under my guidance."', '"One\'s blade is only as sharp as one\'s conviction."\\n—Ajani Goldmane', '"Only fools and bandits use roads."', '"Our law prohibits capital punishment. We believe even the gravest offenders have the chance to redeem themselves."\\n—Torian Sha, soul warden', '"Phirax of Blood Ridge has sent a war giant at us? What, do I have to spell it out for you? Kill the giant, scoop out its skull, and drive it back to Blood Ridge. Honestly, what kind of necromancer minions are you?"\\n—Keren-Dur, necromancer lord', '"Rage courses in every heart, yearning to betray its rational prison."\\n—Sarkhan Vol', '"Rage is a dangerous weapon. Your enemies will try to use your anger against you. Use it against them first."\\n—Ajani Goldmane', '"Sometimes I wonder if our weapons and armor are a step backward."\\n—Soron, rhox pikemaster', '"Stop complaining. You can rest when you\'re dead. Oh—sorry."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"The East Wind, an interloper in the dominions of Westerly Weather, is an impassive-faced tyrant with a sharp poniard held behind his back for a treacherous stab."\\n—Joseph Conrad, *The Mirror of the Sea*', '"The beauty of mental attacks is that your victims never remember them."\\n—Volrath', '"The centaurs are truly free. Never will they be tamed by temptation or controlled by fear. They live in total harmony, a feat not yet achieved by our kind."\\n—Ramal, sage of Westgate', '"The construction of a defense is not accomplished by adding bricks."\\n—Jace Beleren', '"The dead make good soldiers. They can\'t disobey orders, never surrender, and don\'t stop fighting when a random body part falls off."\\n—Nevinyrral, *Necromancer\'s Handbook*', '"The desire for its magic horn inspires such bloodthirsty greed that all who see the unicorn will kill to possess it."\\n—Dionus, elvish archdruid', '"The educated mind is heavy with lore and knowledge. It\'s also the most likely to collapse under its own weight."\\n—Ambassador Laquatus', '"The ground polluted floats with human gore,\\nAnd human carnage taints the dreadful shore\\nFly swift the dangerous coast: let every ear\\nBe stopp\'d against the song! \'tis death to hear!"\\n—Homer, *The Odyssey*, trans. Pope', '"The key to unlocking this puzzle is within you."\\n—Doriel, mentor of Mistral Isle', '"The meadow sprang up beneath me, and I perceived a path from our people\'s defeat to our highest glory."', '"The most disappointing thing about learning telepathy is finding out how boring people really are."\\n—Teferi, fourth-level student', '"The sharks envy our ferocity. The eels envy our cunning."', '"This is a fine suit, armorsmith. I will be safe from harm. If only you could forge rings to mail the rest of my people . . ."\\n—Lord Hilneth', '"This is how wars are won—not with armies of soldiers but with a single knife blade, artfully placed."\\n—Yurin, royal assassin', '"This wound shall be like the chills of winter: swiftly forgotten when spring shoots rise."', '"Those who wish to invade our monastery, please take it up with my servant."\\n—Chandra Nalaar', '"Truth is a straight, keen edge. There are no soft angles or rounded edges. To fight for truth, we must forge in steel."', '"Until that day I cursed the angels, those uncaring lights in the sky. They rewarded my scorn with the gift of time, every year of which I\'ve spent in devotion to their names."\\n—Torian Sha, soul warden', '"We are goblinkind, heirs to the mountain empires of chieftains past. Rest is death to us, and arson is our call to war."', '"We don\'t like interlopers and thieves cluttering our skies."\\n—Dionus, elvish archdruid', '"We see clearly the error of your ways. It does not matter that you choose not to."\\n—Urien of the Lightwielders', '"We\'ll scale these cliffs, traverse Brittle Bridge, and then fight our way down the volcanic slopes on the other side."\\n"Isn\'t the shortest route through the canyon?"\\n"Yes."\\n"So shouldn\'t we—"\\n"No."', '"What am I looking at? Ashes, dead man."', '"What do they see in the throes of panic? I\'m not sure I want to know."\\n—Kezim, prodigal pyromancer', '"When the beast cloaks itself in the mighty oak, what good is a bow? When the oak wraps itself around the snarling beast, what good is a hatchet?"\\n—Dionus, elvish archdruid', '"Where are we? You must learn to ask more useful questions than that."', '"Who\'d want to ignite things one at a time?"\\n—Chandra Nalaar', '"Why fight the body when you can dominate the mind that rules it?"\\n—Jace Beleren', '"You know I accept only one currency here, and yet you have sought me out. Why now do you hesitate?"\\n—Xathrid demon', '"You wish for great destruction? It is done, my master."', '"Your downfall was not your ignorance, your weakness, or your hubris, but your warm blood."\\n—Heidar, Rimewind master', '"Your life will set with the sun."', 'A banner for bonds of blood or belief.', 'A smaller cousin to the dragon, drakes are often seen at the side of powerful wizards who use them as airborne eyes and ears.', 'A typical day for a giant. A momentous event for a goat.', 'A vampire enacts vengeance on the entire world, claiming her debt two tiny pinpricks at a time.', 'A wurm knows nothing of deception. If it opens its mouth, it plans to eat you.', 'After the oryx dies, its flesh returns to the earth, but its emerald bones remain as a tribute to the forest.', 'All are prey to the eyes of the wild.', 'As the glass shattered, forgotten realities and dead memories came flooding back.', "Bears aren't always as strong and as mean as you imagine. Some are even stronger and meaner.", 'Before any major undertaking, a Cylian elf seeks the guidance of a visionary to learn the will of the gargantuan ancients.', 'Bright as a mirror, dark as the sea.', 'Dark thoughts hatch and twist within the mind, straining to take wing.', "Darkness doesn't always send its minions to do its dirty work.", 'Days of planning. Weeks of building. Months of perfecting. Seconds of smashing.', 'Each feather in its tail is a souvenir of an exotic land, a memory condensed in hue.', 'Even the noblest of intentions and strongest of wills inevitably crumble into dust.', "Even when fate is already written, there's always time to change the names.", 'Every grave cradles a recruit.', 'Every living thing has roots in nature. Sometimes nature gets its roots into you.', "Following the sun's cycle, harvest season comes once a year—unless the druids bid the sun behave otherwise.", 'For the first time in his life, Grakk felt a little warm and fuzzy inside.', "Foul-tempered, poorly trained, and mule-stubborn, the drake is the perfect test of the master's will.", 'Fragments of thought refract and multiply, surging in a geyser of dizzying insight.', "From Gaea grew the world, and the world was silent. From Gaea grew the world's elves, and the world was silent no more.\\n—Elvish teaching", "Genius is overrated, especially when it's someone else's.", "Giants and pit spawn attempted to topple the cathedral's pillars. The fine grit of their remains still swirls in the breeze outside.", 'Great generals inspire by example. Goblin chieftains inspire by electrifying the barracks.', 'He knows the name of every elf born in the last four centuries. More importantly, they all know his.', 'He raged at the world, at his family, at his life. But mostly he just raged.', 'Her gaze prevents the petty sins and her sword punishes the rest.', 'Her sword sings more beautifully than any choir.', 'Hunters of every species on the savannah, silvercoats disdain camouflage in favor of total dominance of the food chain.', 'If taken, it cuts the hand that clutches it. If given, it heals the hand that holds it.', 'If you want to destroy something lifeless, make it live.', 'Imitation is the most dangerous form of flattery.', 'In its heart lies the secret of immortality.', 'Ineffable and incorruptible.', 'It disables with pinpoint accuracy.', "It's a mistake to say turtles hide in their shells. They merely need time to contemplate how best to bite your head off.", 'Its curve mimics the twists of life and death.', 'Its diet consists of fruits, plants, small woodland animals, large woodland animals, woodlands, fruit groves, fruit farmers, and small cities.', 'Its form never rests, propelled by some undetectable gale from beyond the gloom.', 'Its victims are known by their eyes: shattered vessels leaking broken dreams.', 'Jariad burned the midnight oil, burned through scroll after scroll, and then burned down his laboratory.', "Just when you thought you'd survived the first wave.", "Keldon warriors don't need signals to tell them when to attack. They need signals to tell them when to stop.", 'Like a meteor, it strikes from above without warning. Unlike a meteor, it then carries you off and eats you.', 'Like all priests, she gives her blessings only to those truly worthy of them.', 'Like nature, the fern spirals back on itself, eternally seeking its own center.', "Mages routinely summon creatures from the Æther. It's only fair that they occasionally throw one back.", 'Masters of the arcane savor a delicious irony. Their study of deep and complex arcana leads to such a simple end: the ability to say merely yes or no.', 'May your weapon be no sword forged. May your armor be no metal wrought.\\n—Elvish saying', 'Mercy is for those who keep their distance.', 'Merfolk are best known for their subtle magic. But those who try to fight them in their own territory quickly realize that merfolk are hardly defenseless on the field of battle.', "Merfolk don't always know what they're looking for, but they're certain once they find it.", 'Most goblins get their turn firing the catapult, but few achieve the coveted title of Ammunition Holder.', "Most knew of the tower's wizard and gargoyle. Few realized which was guardian and which was master.", 'Nature grows solutions to its problems.', "Oddly, no one questioned the Cabal's wisdom in hiring a zombie to work at the cemetery.", 'Once a barbarian army has conquered a region, their shamans summon hellhounds that keep undesirables out and prisoners in.', 'Once a griffin sentinel adopts a territory as its own, only death can force it to betray its post.', "Once he'd worked out which end of the thing was sharp, he was promoted to guard duty.", 'One bone broken for every twig snapped underfoot.\\n—Llanowar penalty for trespassing', 'Regardless of the century, plane, or species, developing artificers never fail to invent the ornithopter.', 'She died in this swamp, and so will you.', 'She shepherds mysteries and dust as others would a flock of sheep.', 'Some angels protect the meek and innocent. Others seek out and smite evil wherever it lurks.', 'Some owls house the souls of archmages of ages past.', 'Some wizards compete not to summon the most interesting creatures, but to create the most interesting aftereffects when a summons goes awry.', 'Sometimes the greatest strength is the strength of conviction.', 'Sparkmages are performance artists of sorts, but pain is the price of admission.', 'The battle was over, but the carnage continued for days.', 'The druids of Mazar treat each seedcone with respect for the warrior it will become.', "The giant spider's silk naturally resists gravity, almost weaving itself as it blankets the forest canopy.", "The horses of Scytha's army must be well trained. A thrown rider would fall miles before meeting the ground.", 'The mage breathed in life-giving air and breathed out death-bringing fire.', 'The mapmaker scowled. He sighed, unrolled his parchment, and painted a large black blob where the Eternal Meadow was once marked.', "The mine's riches never end, nor do the moans of the spirits doomed to haunt them.", 'The more you struggle against its coils, the tighter they get.', 'The most terrifying thing about the craw wurm is probably the horrible crashing sound it makes as it speeds through the forest. This noise is so loud it echoes through the trees and seems to come from all directions at once.', "The murderous horrors of Raven's Run are legendary, but even that haunted place goes quiet when the night wolves howl.", 'The nesting bats of Kelinore sleep soundly while the sun passes, nestled among their grisly collections.', 'The shaman prowled the academy halls, shaking his head at the pomp and babble of the sages inside. He knew just the spell to liven the place up.', "The shapeshifter mimics with a twin's esteem and a mirror's cruelty.", "The sparkmage shrieked, calling on the rage of the storms of his youth. To his surprise, the sky responded with a fierce energy he'd never thought to see again.", 'The spoils of war are not measured only in gold and silver.', 'The thunder of its hooves beats dreams into despair.', 'The undisputed master of the mountains of Shiv.', 'The vanguard is skilled at waging war alone. The enemy is often defeated before its reinforcements reach the front.', 'The void is without substance but cuts like steel.', 'The wise always keep an ear open to the whispers of power.', 'They fell screaming into the depths of the chasm like so many pebbles tossed down a well.', 'They take a blood oath to die in battle. So far none have failed to fulfill the promise.', 'Though no longer attached to the hand, it still holds its adversary in its grasp.', 'Together the soldiers were like a golden blade, cutting down their enemies and scarring the darkness.', 'Tomorrow belongs to those who prepare for it today.', 'Trained in the arts of stealth, royal assassins choose their victims carefully, relying on timing and precision rather than brute force.', 'Viashino lack the majesty of their draconic ancestors, but they lash out with equal rage and twice the spite.', 'Villagers cloaked the town in magical silence, but their ears still bled.', 'When the rhoxes charge, everyone else knows which way to run.', 'When the vaults are empty, everyone is rich.', 'Whether the end comes swift or slow, it always comes too soon.', 'With one flap of her wings, the angel beat back the fires of war.']
artist: ['Adrian Smith', 'Alan Pollack', 'Aleksi Briclot', 'Alex Horley-Orlandelli', 'Andrew Goldhawk', 'Andrew Robinson', 'Ash Wood', 'Austin Hsu', 'Ben Thompson', 'Brian Despain', 'Brian Snõddy', 'Brom', 'Carl Critchlow', 'Chippy', 'Chris Rahn', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Cyril Van Der Haegen', 'D. Alexander Gregory', 'Daarken', 'Dan Dos Santos', 'Dan Frazier', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Daren Bader', 'Darrell Riche', 'Dave Allsop', 'Dave Dorman', 'Dave Kendall', 'David Palumbo', 'Dermot Power', 'DiTerlizzi', 'Don Hazeltine', 'Donato Giancola', 'E. M. Gist', 'Eric Deschamps', 'Eric Fortune', 'Franz Vohwinkel', 'Fred Fields', 'Glen Angus', 'Greg Staples', 'Howard Lyon', 'Izzy', 'Jaime Jones', 'Jason Chan', 'Jeff Miracola', 'Jeremy Jarvis', 'Jesper Ejsing', 'Jim Murray', 'Jim Nelson', 'Jim Pavelec', 'John Avon', 'John Matson', 'Jon Foster', 'Justin Sweet', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Kev Walker', 'Kieran Yanner', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Marcelo Vignali', 'Mark Tedin', 'Mark Zug', 'Martina Pilcerova', 'Matt Cavotta', 'Matt Stewart', 'Matthew D. Wilson', 'Michael Komarck', 'Michael Sutfin', 'Mike Bierek', 'Nick Percival', 'Nils Hamm', 'Paul Bonner', 'Pete Venters', 'Ralph Horsley', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Rebecca Guay', 'Richard Sardinha', 'Rob Alexander', 'Robert Bliss', 'Ron Spencer', 'Ryan Pancoast', 'Sam Wood', 'Scott Bailey', 'Scott M. Fischer', 'Steve Argyle', 'Steve Luke', 'Steve Prescott', 'Steven Belledin', 'Ted Galaday', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Thomas M. Baxa', 'Tim Hildebrandt', 'Todd Lockwood', 'Trevor Claxton', 'Vance Kovacs', 'Volkan Baǵa', 'Véronique Meignaud', 'Warren Mahy', 'Wayne England', 'Wayne Reynolds', 'Zoltan Boros & Gabor Szikszai', 'rk post']
